---
title: Texas Sheet Cake
time: 45 minutes
author: Cheryl Spinner
---

== Cake ==

Preheat #oven to 400°F.

Mix @flour{2%cups} and @sugar{2%cups} in a #large bowl{}.

In a #pot{}, mix @butter{1/2%cup}, @crisco{1/2%cup}, @cocoa{4%tbsp}, and @water{1%cup} and bring to a boil.

Pour over the dry ingredients, stir, and add @buttermilk{3/4%cup}, @vanilla{1%tsp}, @eggs{2}, and @baking soda{1%tsp}. Mix well.

Pour the mixture into a greased #11x14 baking dish{} and bake for ~{15%minutes}.

== Frosting ==

In a #pot{}, mix @butter{1/2%cup}, @cocoa{4%tbsp}, and @milk{1/3%cup} and bring to a boil.

Remove from heat and add @powdered sugar{1%lb}, @vanilla{1%tsp}, and @?chopped nuts{1%cup}. Beat and spread on cake while still hot.
